  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening regional architecture</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian-funded Pacific Security College hosted the inaugural Pacific Regional and National Security Conference in Fiji with nine Pacific partner organisations, and 150 senior representatives of the Pacific security community in June 2024. The Conference featured panels on the Boe Declaration, and a futures exercise on Pacific security cooperation centred on the 2050 Strategy for the Blue Pacific Continent.&#x202f;The Conference reinforced the value of regional action and institutions and fostered regional collaboration across technical sectors. The Conference provided a forum for Pacific security officials and academia to explore ways to further implement the Boe&#x202f;Declaration, and strengthened regional networks.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Security College (the College), in partnership with the Government of Niue and with support from the Government of New Zealand, provided targeted assistance to support the development of Niue&#x2019;s first National Security Strategy (NSS), finalised in May 2025. Engagement began in early 2023, with the College supporting initial consultations and preparatory work involving senior government officials.
&#x200d;
Before the development of the NSS, Niue addressed security issues through sector-led initiatives and agency-level responses. While this enabled progress in specific areas, the NSS introduces a more integrated and coordinated framework to guide national responses to evolving security challenges such as cyber risks, climate change, and transnational crime. It clearly defines national security priorities, institutional responsibilities, and whole-of-government objectives.
&#x200d;
The College supported this process through policy development advice, multi-agency consultations, and alignment with regional frameworks such as the Boe Declaration. It also contributed directly to the translation of the NSS into both English and Vagahau Niue and supported its official publication.
&#x200d;
The strategy is expected to strengthen institutional coordination, policy coherence, and national resilience over the next 3&#x2013;5 years. Evidence of change includes Cabinet approval, a public launch in 2025, and ministerial directives to implement the strategy.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Security College engaged with all Pacific Islands Forum members to deliver eight courses and two workshops on Boe Declaration priorities for Pacific security officials. Courses included, Health and Security, Anchoring Strategic Analysis, Cyber and Technology Security, Regional and National Security Architecture, Pacific Security Policy-Making. These courses aimed to enhance the accountability and governance of Pacific governments across a range of technical security sectors, and built security strategy capabilities. The College also continued to deliver technical assistance to Pacific governments to strengthen national security policy-making and implementation.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
